Deﬁnition 11.1.9 Monofractal function or process
A function or process Xptq in Rd for which hXptq is a constant, @t : hXptq  H, is called monofractal.
Deﬁnition 11.1.10 Multifractal function or process
A function or process Xptq in Rd is called multifractal if it contains more than one Holder exponent h that is living
on a support with non-zero Hausdorff dimension.
All homogeneous processes X with Holder exponents hXpxq not constant have their exponents which are discontinuous everywhere and hence are highly variable and change widely from point to point. As pointed out by Abry et al.
