12.3.2.4
The problem with direction proﬁt
A large number of studies using backpropagation neural networks to forecast ﬁnancial time series are considering
the directional proﬁt (DP) or time dependent directional proﬁt (TDP) models when deﬁning the error function in the
system (see Zhang et al. [2005], Lu Dang Khoa et al. [2006], Wang et al. [2006]). In these studies the function
φpq is assumed to be a penalising coefﬁcient against the wrongly forecasted direction, which is independent of the
actual order of pattern presentation within the learning process. As a result, the standard steepest descent on the error
function is performed, and the weight change is given by
∆Wpt   1q  φT DP ppqη BELS
