12.3.4
Some results
As an example, we consider a training sample made of P  50 pairs with n  4 input Xptq, Xpt  1q, Xpt 
2q, Xpt  3q and m  1 output. The input and target value dptq are described in Table ( 12.1) and Table ( 12.2), where
the index 1, 2, .., 50 corresponds to time t, t  1, ..., t  49. The training sample is plotted in Figure ( 12.4). We use
the translated sigmoid fb,cpq described in Section (13.6.3.3) with bL  1.5 and bH  1.5. Considering a ﬁxed
time window, we test the forecasting power of the model on an out of sample series made of 75 values. We estimate
the point forecast Opt   hq for h  1 and display the results in Table ( 12.3) with index 1, 2, ..., 75 corresponding to
time t   1, t   2, ..., t   75. Accounting for the continually changing nature of ﬁnancial relationships, we deliberately
choose an out of sample series having a very different regime of volatility than the training sample. The true series
and the output of the model are plotted in Figure ( 12.5).
