We can interpret these conditions as
1. Condition 1: The gradient of C, denoted ∇Cpqq is well deﬁned.
2. Condition 2: There can not be more than one way of expressing one’s information. This translate in the convexity
of the cost function given by Equation (13.4.2).
3. Condition 3: It is never possible for a trader to purchase a security bundle r and receive a positive proﬁt regardless of the outcome.
4. Condition 4: The gradient ∇Cpqq represents the traders’ current estimates of the expected payoff of each security denoted by xp.
