13.6.5.2
Backward pass
In general, after a forward pass the network output is not the target input, and we need to measure the distance between
the actual output and the target output to serve as a measurement of the network performance. This distance is called
the error function. Given the input-target pair px, zq, and the network output y, then the error function is given by
