the constraints of the problems called the feasible region. It is deﬁned by the intersection of S and the set of p   q
additional constraints. At any point X P F, the constraints gip.q that satisfy gipXq  0 are active constraints at X
while equality constraints hjp.q are active at all points of F. Many practical problems have objective functions that
are non-differentiable, non-continuous, non-linear, noisy, multi-dimensional and have many local minima. This is the
case of the calibration problem deﬁned in Section (14.2.2).
