14.3.2.5
Simulated annealing
Simulated annealing is a probabilistic optimisation method inspired by the physical process of annealing metals where
a metal is slowly cooled so that its structure is frozen in a minimal energy conﬁguration (see Tsitsiklis et al. [1993]).
